    "result_text": "Done. The build passes with the single acceptance test green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit output confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (REGION=`NSW`, FY=`27`, HASH8=`6E6609E1`, CHK=`1`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**The unified `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`**, computed in `IdentityKeyResolver.deriveMemberId(owner)`:\n- `REGION` \u2014 region code from postcode (or `UNKNOWN`)\n- `FY` \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date\n- `HASH8` \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName) \u2014 the same segment the region-and-hash identity used\n- `CHK` \u2014 a single Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` (reusing `CheckDigitResolver`)\n\n**Files touched:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties; added a single `memberId`; updated the `locality` description.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 renamed field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` (+ getter/setter).\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 renamed the column and widened it to hold the longer id.\n- `IdentityKeyResolver.java` \u2014 `deriveCustomerCode` \u2192 `deriveMemberId` with the new format.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` mappings (`memberId` now maps implicitly from the entity field); `locality`/`timezone` now derive from `memberId`.\n- `LocalityResolver.java` \u2014 extracts `REGION` as the leading letter run (no more `-` separator).\n- `TimezoneResolver.java`, `OwnerSegmentResolver.java` \u2014 now key off `memberId`.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 collision handling (`deriveUniqueMemberId`/`isMemberIdInUse`) applies to `memberId`; audit line references `memberId` (dropped the now-removed membership number); `primaryIdentifier` returns the memberId.\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` \u2014 structured event now emits the identity under the `memberId` JSON key.\n- `CheckDigitResolver.java`, `HexDigest.java` \u2014 doc updates.\n\nThe separate `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `checkDigit` fields are gone; the Luhn digit now lives only as the `CHK` segment inside `memberId`.",
